※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4251
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4251 LANG_LIST_VIEW_WRITTEN

※ **A list is read as a view and never written through one.**  A list is a value: another
※ name may share the room its elements are in as long as neither changes them, and a list in
※ the image is in room nothing may write.  An element written through the list itself copies
※ it out first where it has to; a view is handed where the elements are and no more, so there
※ is nothing to copy out before a write through it.  So a `mut` view is refused one, both as a
※ parameter and as a name.

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[impure]
fn clear(v: mut u8⟦⟧):
    foreach &mut b := v:
        b⌖ ← 0u8

@[startup, impure]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    let l: mut [u8] = [1u8, 2u8, 3u8]
    l ⧺← [4u8]
    clear(l)
    let w: mut u8⟦⟧ = l⟦1…3⟧
    w⟦0⟧ ← 9u8
    if l⟦0⟧ = 0u8: 0u6 else: 1u6
